Review every GitHub issue create, comment, close, and reconciliation route reachable from the changed boundaries. Check that authorization is explicit, test denial overrides inherited live state, and dry-run remains side-effect free. Look for fallback, dedup, rollback, resume, or subprocess paths that bypass the gate or turn refusal into fail-open behavior. Cite every finding with a repository-relative path and line number. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly.
